        "original_id": "9f8ac16a-f651-5db6-ac22-b7ce7d541eec",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Peter Hackett, Captain James Estill\n- Places: Cumberland Gap, Cumberland Mountains, Appalachian Mountains, Virginia, Kentucky, Tennessee\n- Topics: Scotch-Irish migration, Wilderness Road\n\nFacts:\n- In approximately 1771, Peter Hackett was bonded out to Captain James Estill as a boy.\n- In the late 18th century, Peter Hackett was part of the broader Scotch-Irish migration that traveled along the Wilderness Road through the Cumberland Gap from Virginia into what later became known as Kentucky.\n- The Cumberland Gap is a narrow pass through the long ridge of the Cumberland Mountains within the Appalachian Mountains.\n- The Cumberland Gap is near the junction of the U.S. states of Kentucky, Virginia, and Tennessee.",
